  "worked_solution": "First, we must express the series in the form\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{n=1}^{N}{a}_{1}{r}^{n-1},\n$$\n\nwhere ${a}_{1}$ denotes the first term of the series, $r$ denotes the common ratio, and $N$ denotes the number of terms in the series. In this case, ${a}_{1}=6,$ $r=-4$ and $N=32.$\n\nExpressing the geometric series in sigma notation, we obtain:\n\n$$\n{S}_{32}={\\sum }_{n=1}^{32}6{(-4)}^{n-1}\\,\\,\n$$\n\nFinally, we can simplify the above using the laws of exponents, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{n=1}^{32}6{(-4)}^{n-1} & ={\\sum }_{n=1}^{32}6{(-4)}^{n}{(-4)}^{-1} \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{n=1}^{32}6{(-4)}^{n}(-\\frac{1}{4}) \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{n=1}^{32}(-\\frac{3}{2}){(-4)}^{n}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
